& git pull -q $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git; git log --format='%h %s' | head -3; git diff HEAD~2 HEAD | head -80; cd /hutian/idea-wiki && git pull -q $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git; git log --fo…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/story-wiki && git pull -q $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/story-repo.wiki.git; git log --format='%h %s' | head -3; git diff HEAD~2 HEAD | head -80; cd /hutian/idea-wiki && git pull -q $HT_FORGEJO_URL/world/idea-repo.wiki.git; git log --format='%h %s' | head -2; cd /hutian/experiment-repo && git pull -q; git log --format='%h %s' | head -3; cd /hutian/figtab-repo && git pull -q; git log --format='%h %s' | head -3"]], "output": "```console\n55ae7df Tidy the outline header\n10064e1 Outline rev 6: hold the extrapolation headline for the Brief's recalibrated estimator; mark it post-results\n84d777b Outline rev 5: selection by leave-one-benchmark-out, scope of the tuning finding, distance in the headline\ndiff --git a/Outline.md b/Outline.md\nindex 4cf3da5..02974d5 100644\n--- a/Outline.md\n+++ b/Outline.md\n@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n-# Outline (revision 5, after idea-review #5; revision 4 was after idea-review #3, venue #4 and the first full results of analysis, `experiment-repo`#5, results-v1) — story-repo\n+# Outline (revision 6): after the idea review, the venue request, results-v1 and Brief rev 3 — story-repo\n \n-Working from: `Brief` of idea-repo (revision 2), objective `story-repo#1`. This page says **what to test and what each part of the paper says**; it never says what a result must be. Where a result decides between two stories, both are written below (§6) so nobody has to rewrite the paper's frame after the fact.\n+Working from: `Brief` of idea-repo (revision 3), objective `story-repo#1`. This page says **what to test and what each part of the paper says**; it never says what a result must be. Where a result decides between two stories, both are written below (§6) so nobody has to rewrite the paper's frame after the fact.\n \n ## Venue frame (venue-repo, `story-repo`#4)\n NeurIPS 2026 Main Track; **9 content pages including figures and tables**; references, appendix and checklist outside. **Contribution type: General** (an evaluation paper: controlled comparison, bias–variance accounting, ceiling analysis), also if the headline turns out conditional or negative: \"Negative Results\" is not chosen (high significance/originality bar). **Main body: 7 items** — Fig. 1, Table 2, Fig. 2, Fig. 3, Fig. 4, Fig. 5, Fig. 6 (Fig. 1 is a small schematic). Everything else is appendix: Table 1 (audit and split/target counts), Table 3, Table 4, Fig. 5b, per-benchmark tables. Evidence a claim rests on is in the main body: the main text carries the k targets / #families per split in Table 2's columns and one sentence on thin cells, and says where Table 1 is. Writing profile: abstract one paragraph ≈ 130–260 words stating claims, scope and the headline; introduction ≈ 550–1500 words with the result stated; first figure on page 1–2; short related work in the main text, long version in the appendix; the checklist's \"Claims\" item is checked against the evidence.\n@@ -67,7 +67,8 @@ The abstract's headline is the **single main result** (tested on the extrapolati\n \n ## 6b. Where the evidence stands (analysis, results-v1; numbers are analysis's, check against its `results/` before use)\n The outline's ending is now decided in outline, pending the 2% block, the source-count block and a higher-draw run:\n-- **Headline (one main result, extrapolation split):** *source models help most when the target resembles them; for targets above every source, pure model-based predictors lose to plain sampling by bias (RMSE ≈ 1.5–2× uniform at n = 100); the difference estimator removes that bias; what is left over uniform is mostly design (stratified/balanced sampling), and over stratified sampling the gain is small or gone (CI includes 1 for diff-irt).* In interpolation/lineage the gain from sources is large (≈ 0.65–0.70 of uniform's RMSE, ≈ 0.8 of stratified's).\n+- **HOLD (Brief rev 3):** the extrapolation paragraph below is provisional until analysis answers the Brief's §3b/§3c additions (target-recalibrated regression with a slope fitted on the target's own n answers, an optional two-phase design) and the check whether the model-based predictors' extrapolation failure is partly the ability prior's shrinkage. Interpolation/lineage statements and the ceiling are unaffected. The recalibrated estimator was **added after seeing results-v1**, motivated by the tuned-λ failure; the paper says so (pre-registration language) and lists it as post-results. Wording for extrapolation as the Brief puts it: the value of diff\n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "682ff1e5-6be9-5d07-a167-9f0e4e752a27", "at": 1795676575.867795, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 26448, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "paper-repo", "actor": "paper-repo", "execution_id": "0f8840c99f7596269aefdaef3989cbf3", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "454e37ad-be7a-566e-93ef-dd4fc043aa61", "at": 1795676575.8716097, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 26449, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "paper-repo", "actor": "paper-repo", "execution_id": "0f8840c99f7596269aefdaef3989cbf3", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "d3d463c7-6130-533b-a7d4-797c6aa8990a", "at": 1795676575.875212, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 26450, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "paper-repo", "actor": "paper-repo", "execution_id": "0f8840c99f7596269aefdaef3989c